virglrenderer: emulate dma_buf for Venus where memory is shm imported as host memory (macOS).
The guest Venus driver only exposes external memory (needed by compositors and Zink) when the renderer
has VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf, which macOS drivers cannot have. With use_host_memory_import:
- advertise VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf, VK_EXT_queue_family_foreign and
  VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier (linear modifier only), next to the injected
  VK_KHR_external_memory_fd (Zink needs them for dma_buf), and keep them, and the dma_buf/opaque
  fd handle types, away from the driver;
- answer external buffer/image queries for them, and create shareable images linear (shm holds
  linear images only; their layout is opaque to the guest);
- exportable memory is shm-backed (host-visible type), already exported as VIRGL_RESOURCE_FD_SHM;
- importing an shm resource imports its mapping as host memory; shm resources exported from
  device memory now hold a mapping too, like imported ones (the union held an fd there).
Similar in spirit to the draft !1586 (emulate unsupported extensions), much smaller.

